confirmed.fix:
Let the password cross ':' again: `([^\s/]{1,256})@((?:[a-z][\w-]{0,31})?\(|\/)`. That is 4a284f9's class, now with '@', so it keeps 'up to the last @'.

My fix/ copy:
- passes all 71 head data-diff tests, including the 'a:' <1 s test (193 ms);
- masks every shape above;
- shows 0 fuzz regressions against 4a284f9 and 7193877 (70K cases).

256 KB of 'a:' costs 174 ms CPU, the same as 4a284f9's 168 ms (W28=B: document in the README limit). Remove 'a DSN password with a `:`' from the misses, and add a test with `root:…:…@tcp(…)` and `root:…:@tcp(…)`.

confirmed.evidence:
The cause is `DSN_USERINFO = /(?<![\w.-])([\w.-]{1,64}):([^\s/:]{1,256})@(…)/gi`; at 4a284f9 the class was `[^\s@/]`. The run now stops at the next ':', so the user/password split lands mid-password, or nothing matches at all.

corpus.mjs (out-corpus.txt), neutral field 'note'. Each line gives 4a284f9 → 4ed6449:
- `root:Zq9SeCr3tVal:@tcp(127.0.0.1:3306)/app`: `root:[secret 3e08ba37]@tcp(…)` → shown as is, the whole password in clear;
- `root::Zq9SeCr3tVal@tcp(…)`: masked → whole in clear;
- `root:Zq9Se:Cr3tVal@tcp(…)`: masked → `root:Zq9Se:[secret a7f1ce1f]@tcp(…)`, the first part in clear;
- the same for `@unix(…)`, `@udp(…)`, and a log line `dsn root:Zq9Se:Cr3tVal@tcp(db:3306)/app?parseTime=true`.

fuzz-dsn.mjs (out-fuzz-dsn.txt): 6,000 DSNs whose passwords use a generator's usual symbol set. Of the 889 passwords that hold ':', 153 show whole and 307 in part at 4ed6449; 4a284f9 masked all 460. Example: `root:]p3j5a,!VV!:z<h{=dL@tcp(db:3306)/app` is fully in clear.

Whole-text masking catches only a DSN behind a secret-looking key (`dsn=…`). It misses one under a JSON key such as `mysql` or in a log line.

Why this counts as a regression although README:419 lists it: README:419 now lists 'a DSN password with a `:` in it' among the misses, and the reply calls the ':' mutant one that 'masks no less, and only costs time'. Narrowing the class was a trade for the round-5 perf nit. W28=B makes perf document-only, and this un-masks values 4a284f9 masked.

